target/
cs3_windows/dist-electron/

# Portable JDK 21 + Maven fetched to build the sidecar. Downloaded, never
# vendored: ~250 MB of third-party binaries do not belong in git history.
tools/toolchain/
# Harness and packaging output. `provider-e2e.mjs --json` writes wherever you
# point it, `build-runtime.mjs` assembles ~90 MB into sidecar/dist (already
# covered by the `dist` rule above), and the sidecar writes a scratch data dir
# when run directly rather than through Electron.
e2e-*.json
e2e-*.log
sidecar/plugin-data/

.github/hooks/context-mode.json
.temp/
cs3_windows/release
# `cs3-sidecar.jar` unzipped in place. A `jar xf` at the repo root leaves
# `META-INF/` and `com/` beside the sources they were compiled from, and one
# merge carried all 28 of them into the tree — build output that goes stale
# silently and reads, to anyone who finds it, like a second copy of the sidecar.
# Anchored: `com/` unanchored would reach every `com` directory at any depth,
# which is the rule shape that once swallowed `src/components/extensions/`.
/META-INF/
/com/
